# Project-Specific (Data & Logs)
data/
logs/
*.log

# Per-backend run output — one entry per path a config or the test suite writes
# to, so a run of ANY backend leaves the tree clean. Grep the example configs for
# `save_dir` / `filename` / `fname` / `checkpoint_dir` / `export_dir` before
# adding a backend, and add its path here in the same change.
lightning_logs/
# The marainer tracker default: `save_dir` is declared ONCE on the `Tracker` ABC as
# "./runs", so every backend (csv / tensorboard / mlflow / aim / clearml / wandb) lands
# here when a config omits it — and wandb nests its own directory inside, so this one
# entry covers all of them. A tracker pointed at an explicit `save_dir` (the example
# config's ./lightning_logs, or a $VAR outside the repo) never reaches it.
runs/
keras_logs/
tensorflow_logs/
fastai_logs/
# `examples/sweep/run_sweep.sh` writes here: the per-run training logs it names in its
# summary, the file-backed trackers' output (`--tracker csv` / `tensorboard` / `aim`), the
# TensorFlow SavedModel export and the HuggingFace Trainer's state. All of it is a sweep's
# by-product; the RESULTS live in whichever tracker the sweep was pointed at.
sweep_logs/
torch_runs/
hf_runs/
exported/
checkpoints/
_sonair_test_logs/

# Reports (regenerated by CI — Jenkinsfile / GH Actions)
*-checkstyle.xml
*-diff.txt
flake8.txt
mypy.txt
coverage.xml
coverage-sources.zip
test-report.xml

# Pretrained model caches (downloaded by timm at first use)
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
.cache/
/pyrightconfig.json
